Subject: [PATCH] lib: backport libyang 4/5/6 API compatibility to FRR 10.4.5

Keep FRR 10.4.5 and use the newer libyang API. Adapt the existing callsites
using the upstream FRR migrations: 908b162fcae696eac6a3b923f6d2004a2a74931f,
ca824ba98a274d335e53303ed3ee367f6dea2e2b,
1e4957e03f845f4eea8cda232d8f30db1424ebda, and
e5da38bfc92fb08e990b5dbf061787c08616c976. The uint32/uint64 canonical-value
helpers follow upstream's current implementations without changing the
10.4.5 callback API. Existing path constructors use zero lengths, so their
byte-to-bit API change does not alter values.

Replace direct parent-structure accesses with the public parent/child API,
handle schema defaults and renamed flags, and preserve ordinary LYB
printing/parsing behavior. Replace the removed binary term constructor with
canonical integer strings and adapt its ordinary regression fixture.

This is a FRR compatibility patch. The libyang source security fixes are
tracked and applied separately.

